.TH smi-pki-server-extensions "1" "September 2026" "SMI Toolset" "SMI PKI Command"
.SH NAME
smi-pki-server-extensions \- Write server certificate OpenSSL extensions to a file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smi-pki-server-extensions
.I OUT_EXT_FILE SAN
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Writes the server extensions to \fIOUT_EXT_FILE\fR for \fISAN\fR (for example \fBDNS:ldap.has.ee.gintra\fR): basicConstraints=critical,CA:FALSE, keyUsage=critical,digitalSignature,keyEncipherment, extendedKeyUsage=serverAuth, subjectKeyIdentifier=hash, authorityKeyIdentifier=keyid,issuer, and the subjectAltName.
It is a thin command line wrapper over the matching function in the file based PKI library
\fBpki.sh\fR, so each step of building a CA and signing certificates can be run and inspected
on its own. All material is passed as file names; the command fails if the underlying OpenSSL
operation fails.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR smi-pki-ca-create (1),
.BR smi-pki-create-domain-cert (1),
.BR openssl (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Imre Tabur <imre.tabur@mail.ee>
